{
  "statement": "offload files first and then may ask for one field the row genuinely needs and nothing gave it: the dates of a stay, the by-when of a reminder, a deadline, a gift or a renewal, the time of a meeting or call, or the tag a thread's notes say rows carry. It never asks what they meant, what kind of row it is or where it goes; never a field already given; at most two in a turn, dates before tags; options are values it already holds; and a note can require or forbid a question.",
  "why": "An unanswered question costs nothing, so a question is only worth asking about a field the row needs. A wrong home is one move away and a wrong kind is corrected by the way out, so neither is asked. Where the notes give the answer, asking is filing by another name.",
